From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: keep the Q25 panel powered so double-tap can wake it

0906 dropped the panel's board_name, as the stock brightness dtbo does.
The panel driver uses that name only at screen off: without it, it pulls
the panel's reset (GPIO 85) and avdd (GPIO 156) low. On the owner's Q25
(2026-11-14) dmesg showed the touch driver arm double-tap to wake and the
panel power off 30 ms later ("Q20 V1 board poweroff"); after that a double
tap raised no touch interrupt at all, so the touch controller had been
reset out of its wakeup-gesture mode. Put board_name back so the panel
stays powered in sleep mode at screen off, as it did before 0906. The
PWM backlight changes from 0906 are unchanged.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/q20_v12_factory.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/q20_v12_factory.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/q20_v12_factory.dts
index e26e079..14b449d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/q20_v12_factory.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/q20_v12_factory.dts
@@ -144,6 +144,13 @@
 		reg = <0>;
 		reset-gpios = <&pio 85 0>;
 		avdd-gpios  = <&pio 156 0>;
+		/*
+		 * SableOS: keep the panel's reset and power up at screen off. Without
+		 * this name the panel driver drops reset (GPIO 85) and avdd (GPIO 156)
+		 * when the screen turns off, which also resets the touch controller,
+		 * so it loses double-tap to wake mode and no tap is seen.
+		 */
+		board_name = "q20_v12";
 		port {
 			panel_in1: endpoint {
 				remote-endpoint = <&dsi_out>;
